Kernel (SiliconForest 0e1f46661376 + the M3 tree patch), asahi-m3 G15, on top of
patches/g15-perf-tgt-util.patch and patches/g15-recovery-drain-halt.patch: three module parameters for
the firmware DVFS performance controller words, all default 0 = unchanged.
  asahi.g15_perf_boost_min    HardwareDataA +0x790, boost minimum utilization, percent (template 90; 30..100)
  asahi.g15_perf_boost_step   HardwareDataA +0x794, boost step, apple,perf-boost-ce-step (template 50; 10..100)
  asahi.g15_perf_base_pstate  HardwareDataA +0x7d8/+0x7e0/+0x81c = 100 x base and +0x7d4 = (top - base) / 0.95
                              as f32 (template base 1; 1..7)
The offsets and the base-state formula are the ones g15/board/record.rs writes. Each override is refused
(probe fails, the next boot is normal) unless its words hold the template values. The meaning of the
boost words comes from their device-tree names; the unit of the step is not known.
